    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate a comprehensive summary of the following content.\n\nContent Type: {{ $json.contentType }}\nLanguage: {{ $json.language }}\nContent:\n{{ $json.enrichedContent }}\n\nIMPORTANT: Use the web_search tool to find 2-3 additional recent facts or context about the main topic before writing. Use wikipedia to verify key facts.\n\nProvide a well-structured summary in {{ $json.language }} that covers all key points and main ideas. Use markdown formatting with headers (##), bullet points, and bold text for important terms. Include:\n- An overview paragraph\n- Key takeaways\n- Any relevant recent context found via web search",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expert educator and content summarizer. You have access to web search and Wikipedia tools — always use them to enrich your summaries with current, factual information. Create clear, comprehensive summaries. Always respond in the language specified by the user."
        }
      },
      "id": "e9736a3a-83aa-40b4-b810-ae21d5ea30c7",
      "name": "Summary Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        144
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate detailed, structured study notes for the following content.\n\nContent Type: {{ $json.contentType }}\nLanguage: {{ $json.language }}\nContent:\n{{ $json.enrichedContent }}\n\nIMPORTANT: Use the web_search tool to find supplementary explanations, and use wikipedia to look up definitions of any key terms before writing notes.\n\nCreate detailed study notes in {{ $json.language }} with the following structure:\n- Use ## for main topics and ### for subtopics\n- Include definitions, explanations, and examples enriched with real web sources\n- Highlight key terms in **bold**\n- Use numbered lists for sequential information\n- Use bullet points for non-sequential details\n- Add a 'Key Concepts' section at the end\n- Add a 'Further Reading' section with 2-3 real sources found via web search",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expert note-taker and educator. You have access to web search and Wikipedia — always use them to add real examples, definitions, and sources to your notes. Always respond in the language specified by the user."
        }
      },
      "id": "14704873-57d0-4539-87f7-b1c0f2e99ee0",
      "name": "Notes Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate an interactive quiz based on the following content.\n\nContent Type: {{ $json.contentType }}\nLanguage: {{ $json.language }}\nContent:\n{{ $json.enrichedContent }}\n\nIMPORTANT: Use web_search and wikipedia to verify that all answers and facts in your questions are 100% accurate before generating the quiz.\n\nCreate exactly 5 multiple choice questions in {{ $json.language }}. Each question must have exactly 4 options. Make questions progressively harder. Test understanding, not just recall.\n\nYou MUST respond with ONLY valid JSON in this exact format (no markdown, no code blocks, no extra text):\n{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"...\",\"options\":[\"...\",\"...\",\"...\",\"...\"],\"correctAnswer\":\"...\",\"explanation\":\"...\"}]}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expert quiz maker. You have access to web search and Wikipedia — always use them to verify facts before creating questions. Create challenging but accurate MCQs. Always respond in the language specified. Return ONLY valid JSON."
        }
      },
      "id": "54b0d10d-3b1a-494f-89ba-64dc81997e55",
      "name": "Quiz Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        656
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate flashcards based on the following content.\n\nContent Type: {{ $json.contentType }}\nLanguage: {{ $json.language }}\nContent:\n{{ $json.enrichedContent }}\n\nIMPORTANT: Use wikipedia to look up precise definitions and use web_search to find real-world examples for the back of each flashcard.\n\nCreate exactly 8 flashcards in {{ $json.language }}. Each flashcard should cover a distinct concept. The front should be a question or term, the back should be a concise but complete answer enriched with a real-world example where possible.\n\nYou MUST respond with ONLY valid JSON in this exact format (no markdown, no code blocks, no extra text):\n{\"cards\":[{\"front\":\"...\",\"back\":\"...\"}]}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an expert educator specializing in spaced repetition learning. You have access to web search and Wikipedia — always use them to create accurate, example-rich flashcards. Always respond in the language specified. Return ONLY valid JSON."
        }
      },
      "id": "5a3c1827-15cb-41b3-98a9-539d85b6509e",
